  "limitations": [
    "This is a static review of one exact rendered manifest, not a Kubernetes admission, runtime or penetration test.",
    "The privileged node driver, /dev access, k0s host paths and bidirectional kubelet mount are expected CSI capabilities but remain high-trust boundaries requiring live qualification.",
    "The controller service-account token is shared by all containers in the controller pod because the upstream chart does not isolate projected tokens per sidecar.",
    "The node DaemonSet selects a dedicated ServiceAccount with automatic API-token mounts disabled; this static control still requires a live compatibility test.",
    "RuntimeDefault seccomp is set at pod level for controller and node workloads. Kubernetes privileged-container semantics mean this does not constrain the privileged node driver; that exception remains a live qualification boundary.",
    "Empty resource constraints and unenforced container-level security contexts require measured hardening before production use."
  ]
